,"title":"Association of Thyroid Peroxidase Antibodies and Thyroglobulin Antibodies with Thyroid Function in Pregnancy : An Individual Participant Data Meta-Analysis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-499747","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"CONTEXT: Interpretation of thyroid function tests during pregnancy is limited by the generalizability of reference intervals between cohorts due to inconsistent methodology. OBJECTIVE: (1) To provide an overview of published reference intervals for thyrotropin (TSH) and free thyroxine (FT4) in pregnancy, (2) to assess the consequences of common methodological between-study differences by combining raw data from different cohorts. METHODS: (1) Ovid MEDLINE, EMBASE, and Web of Science were searched until December 12, 2021. Studies were assessed in duplicate. (2) The individual participant data (IPD) meta-analysis was performed in participating cohorts in the Consortium on Thyroid and Pregnancy. RESULTS: (1) Large between-study methodological differences were identified, 11 of 102 included studies were in accordance with current guidelines; (2) 22 cohorts involving 63 198 participants were included in the meta-analysis. Not excluding thyroid peroxidase antibody-positive participants led to a rise in the upper limits of TSH in all cohorts, especially in the first (mean +17.4%; range +1.6 to +30.3%) and second trimester (mean +9.8%; range +0.6 to +32.3%). The use of the 95th percentile led to considerable changes in upper limits, varying from -10.8% to -21.8% for TSH and -1.2% to -13.2% for FT4. All other additional exclusion criteria changed reference interval cut-offs by a maximum of 3.5%. Applying these findings to the 102 studies included in the systematic review, 48 studies could be used in a clinical setting. CONCLUSION: We provide an overview of clinically relevant reference intervals for TSH and FT4 in pregnancy. The results of the meta-analysis indicate that future studies can adopt a simplified study setup without additional exclusion criteria.","author_count":49,"contributors":["Osinga, Joris A.J.","Derakhshan, Arash","Palomaki, Glenn E.","Ashoor, Ghalia","Männistö, Tuija","Maraka, Spyridoula","Chen, Liangmiao","Bliddal, Sofie","Lu, Xuemian","Taylor, Peter N.","Vrijkotte, Tanja G.M.","Tao, Fang Biao","Brown, Suzanne J.","Ghafoor, Farkhanda","Poppe, Kris","Veltri, Flora","Chatzi, Lida","Vaidya, Bijay","Broeren, Maarten A.C.","Shields, Beverley M.","Itoh, Sachiko","Mosso, Lorena","Popova, Polina V.","Anopova, Anna D.","Kishi, Reiko","Aminorroaya, Ashraf","Kianpour, Maryam","López-Bermejo, Abel","Oken, Emily","Pirzada, Amna","Vafeiadi, Marina","Bramer, Wichor M.","Suvanto, Eila","Yoshinaga, Jun","Huang, Kun","Bassols, Judit","Boucai, Laura","Feldt-Rasmussen, Ulla","Grineva, Elena N.","Pearce, Elizabeth N.","Alexander, Erik K.","Pop, Victor J.M.","Nelson, Scott M.","Walsh, John P.","Peeters, Robin P.","Chaker, Layal","Nicolaides, Kypros H.","D'Alton, Mary E.","Korevaar, Tim I.M."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-434124"],"filters":{"added":"2022-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","America, South","Asia, East","Asia, Middle East","Asia, South","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia","Belgium","Chile","China","Finland","Greece","Iran","Japan","Netherlands","Pakistan","Russia","Spain","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Almazov National Medical Research Centre","Anhui Medical University","Boston University","Brown University","Cardiff University","Columbia University","Cornell University","Erasmus University Rotterdam","Harvard University","Hokkaido University","Isfahan University of Medical Sciences","King's College Hospital NHS Foundation Trust","King's College London","Maxima Medical Centre","Mayo Clinic Rochester, MN","Pavlov First State Medical University of St. Petersburg","Pontificia Universidad Católica de Chile","Saint-Pierre University Hospital","Shalamar Institute of Health Sciences","Shifa International Hospital","Sir Charles Gairdner Hospital","Tilburg University","Toyo University","University of Amsterdam","University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences","University of Crete","University of Exeter","University of Girona","University of Glasgow","University of Oulu","University of Southern California","University of Western Australia","Wenzhou Medical University"],"keyword":["Pregnancy","Reference Values","Thyroid"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tsh and ft000000000004 reference intervals in pregnancy a systematic review and individual participant data meta analysis","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1210/clinem/dgac425","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-434124","identifier":[{"id":"PMC9516198","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85139375230","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35861700","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-441e9fc0-4b30-4bc2-b1ed-c09e1bb57734"],"keyword":["free thyroxine (FT4)","pregnancy","reference values","thyroid","thyrotropin (TSH)"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CF57C1C0D11B478F29E5B61E19FE2C3C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/323997827/dgac425.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1210/clinem/dgac425","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"nl","key":"erasmus university rotterdam","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Erasmus University Rotterdam","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"brown university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Brown University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"king s college hospital nhs f