{"abstract":"There has been much recent interest in the concept of rewilding as a tool for nature conservation, but also confusion over the idea, which has limited its utility. We developed a unifying definition and 10 guiding principles for rewilding through a survey of 59 rewilding experts, a summary of key organizations’ rewilding visions, and workshops involving over 100 participants from around the world. The guiding principles convey that rewilding exits on a continuum of scale, connectivity, and level of human influence and aims to restore ecosystem structure and functions to achieve a self-sustaining autonomous nature. These principles clarify the concept of rewilding and improve its effectiveness as a tool to achieve global conservation targets, including those of the UN Decade on Ecosystem Restoration and post-2020 Global Biodiversity Framework. Finally, we suggest differences in rewilding perspectives lie largely in the extent to which it is seen as achievable and in specific interventions. An understanding of the context of rewilding projects is the key to success, and careful site-specific interpretations will help achieve the aims of rewilding.","author_count":33,"contributors":["Carver, Steve","Convery, Ian","Hawkins, Sally","Beyers, Rene","Eagle, Adam","Kun, Zoltan","Van Maanen, Erwin","Cao, Yue","Fisher, Mark","Edwards, Stephen R.","Nelson, Cara","Gann, George D.","Shurter, Steve","Aguilar, Karina","Andrade, Angela","Ripple, William J.","Davis, John","Sinclair, Anthony","Bekoff, Marc","Noss, Reed","Foreman, Dave","Pettersson, Hanna","Root-Bernstein, Meredith","Svenning, Jens Christian","Taylor, Peter","Wynne-Jones, Sophie","Featherstone, Alan Watson","Fløjgaard, Camilla","Stanley-Price, Mark","Navarro, Laetitia M.","Aykroyd, Toby","Parfitt, Alison","Soulé, Michael"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-165967"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","America, South","Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Carver, Steve"],"country":["Chile","China","France","Germany","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Bangor University","German Centre for Integrative Biodiversity Research (iDiv)","Martin Luther University Halle-Wittenberg","National Natural History Museum","Oregon State University","Tsinghua University","Universidad Austral de Chile","University of California at Berkeley","University of Colorado Boulder","University of Cumbria","University of Leeds","University of Montana","University of Oxford"],"keyword":["Definition","Ecosystem management","Goals","Guiding principles","Rewilding"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"guiding principles for rewilding","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/cobi.13730","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-165967","identifier":[{"id":"85107124810","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000657604100001","type":"wos"},{"id":"33728690","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-40558f21-f388-4856-b5bc-2f0fb1a5052e"],"keyword":["definition","ecosystem management","goals","guiding principles","rewilding"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0D526B02008BA505D5C890825C789809"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/cobi.13730","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/273853254/Conservation_Biology_2021_Carver_Guiding_principles_for_rewilding.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology 