{"abstract":"The heart of the scientific enterprise is a rational effort to understand the causes behind the phenomena we observe. In large-scale complex dynamical systems such as the Earth system, real experiments are rarely feasible. However, a rapidly increasing amount of observational and simulated data opens up the use of novel data-driven causal methods beyond the commonly adopted correlation techniques. Here, we give an overview of causal inference frameworks and identify promising generic application cases common in Earth system sciences and beyond. We discuss challenges and initiate the benchmark platform causeme.net to close the gap between method users and developers.","author_count":21,"contributors":["Runge, Jakob","Bathiany, Sebastian","Bollt, Erik","Camps-Valls, Gustau","Coumou, Dim","Deyle, Ethan","Glymour, Clark","Kretschmer, Marlene","Mahecha, Miguel D.","Muñoz-Marí, Jordi","van Nes, Egbert H.","Peters, Jonas","Quax, Rick","Reichstein, Markus","Scheffer, Marten","Schölkopf, Bernhard","Spirtes, Peter","Sugihara, George","Sun, Jie","Zhang, Kun","Zscheischler, Jakob"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-489983"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Netherlands","Spain","Switzerland","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Carnegie Mellon University","Clarkson University","ETH Zürich","German Aerospace Center","Helmholtz-Zentrum Hereon","Imperial College London","Max Planck Institute for Biogeochemistry","Max Planck Institute for Intelligent Systems","Nutrition and Food Science Area","Potsdam Institute for Climate Impact Research","University of Amsterdam","University of Bern","University of California at San Diego","Vrije Universiteit Amsterdam","Wageningen University & Research"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-