{"abstract":"We demonstrate the use of a C0 discontinuous Galerkin method for topology optimization of nano-mechanical sensors, namely temperature, surface stress, and mass sensors. The sensors are modeled using classical thin plate theory, which requires C1 basis functions in the standard finite element method. A discontinuous Galerkin type approach allows the use of C0 basis functions or any common basis functions, e.g. based on Lagrange elements. Thus the implementation is simple and requires fewer degrees of freedom per element compared to common finite element implementation of plate problems.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Marhadi, Kun Saptohartyadi","Evgrafov, Anton","Sørensen, Mads Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-323882"],"event":{"end":"2011-06-17","place":"Shizuoka, jp","start":"2011-06-13","title":"9th World Congress on Structural and Multidisciplinary Optimization","year":"2011"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Discontinuous Galerkin method","Thin plates","Topology optimization"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"topology optimization of nano mechanical cantilever sensors using a c000000000000 discontinuous galerkin type approach","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.wcsmo9.com/","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-323882","ids":["dtu-40eac415-fc48-49f9-b0ad-599969c2aaa9"],"keyword":["Discontinuous Galerkin method","Nano-mechanical sensors","Thin plates","Topology optimization"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-7BEE61D286A5FED7A0DB44F34042A200"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.wcsmo9.com/","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Mathematics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kun Saptohartyadi","key":"marhadipau","last":"Marhadi","locid":"3b1a221d-7a54-4194-9514-9da48606a97b","name":"Marhadi, Kun Saptohartyadi","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anton","key":"evgrafovpau","last":"Evgrafov","locid":"5b5c3973-511e-41e0-b0f4-e6f7dce2c1d4","name":"Evgrafov, Anton","orcid":"0000-0002-3987-7745","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mads Peter","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"651b67f7-1e41-4719-8369-01b34075cd6b","name":"Sørensen, Mads Peter","orcid":"0000-0003-0820-8722","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 9th World Congress on Structural and Multidisciplinary Optimization"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-40eac415-fc48-49f9-b0ad-599969c2aaa9"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Topology Optimization of Nano-Mechanical Cantilever Sensors Using a C0 Discontinuous Galerkin-Type Approach","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-323882","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
